narrative">Kennedy Center &middot; September 17, 2026</p><h1 data-layer="fact">The judge required notice before a Kennedy Center demolition</h1><p class="story-dek" data-layer="fact">The September 17 order denied an emergency hearing but required written notice more than 30 days before the defendants implement a change to the project plans previously presented to the court, including demolition of the main building. It did not decide whether demolition would be lawful.</p><div class="mode-switcher" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Reading mode"><a class="mode-btn active" href="?mode=story" data-mode="story" role="radio" aria-checked="true">The story</a><a class="mode-btn" href="?mode=facts" data-mode="facts" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Just the facts</a><a class="mode-btn" href="?mode=work" data-mode="work" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Show the work</a></div><script type="module">document.addEventListener(`DOMContentLoaded`,()=>{let e=document.getElementById(`story-root`),t=document.querySelectorAll(`.mode-btn`);if(!e||!t.length)return;let n=new URLSearchParams(window.location.search),r=[`story`,`facts`,`work`].includes(n.get(`mode`))?n.get(`mode`):`story`;e.classList.add(`mode-${r}`);let i=e.querySelector(`[data-record-ledger]`);i&&(i.open=r===`work`),t.forEach(e=>{let t=e.getAttribute(`data-mode`)===r;e.classList.toggle(`active`,t),e.setAttribute(`aria-checked`,t?`true`:`false`),e.setAttribute(`tabindex`,t?`0`:`-1`)}),t.forEach((n,r)=>{n.addEventListener(`keydown`,e=>{let n=e.key===`ArrowRight`||e.key===`ArrowDown`?1:e.key===`ArrowLeft`||e.key===`ArrowUp`?-1:0;if(!n&&e.key!==`Home`&&e.key!==`End`&&e.key!==` `)return;e.preventDefault();let i=e.key===`Home`?t[0]:e.key===`End`?t[t.length-1]:t[(r+n+t.length)%t.length];i.click(),i.focus()}),n.addEventListener(`click`,r=>{r.preventDefault();let a=[...e.querySelectorAll(`section[id], aside[id]`)],o=a.find(e=>`#`+e.id===location.hash&&e.getBoundingClientRect().top>=0&&e.getBoundingClientRect().top<innerHeight)??a.filter(e=>e.getBoundingClientRect().height&&e.getBoundingClientRect().top<=160).at(-1),s=n.getAttribute(`data-mode`);i&&(i.open=s===`work`),e.className=e.className.replace(/mode-\w+/g,``).trim()+` mode-${s}`,t.forEach(e=>{let t=e===n;e.classList.toggle(`active`,t),e.setAttribute(`aria-checked`,t?`true`:`false`),e.setAttribute(`tabindex`,t?`0`:`-1`)});let c=new URL(window.location.href);if(c.searchParams.set(`mode`,s),o){let e=a.indexOf(o),t=o.getBoundingClientRect().height?o:[...a.slice(0,e).reverse(),...a.slice(e+1)].find(e=>e.getBoundingClientRect().height);t&&(requestAnimationFrame(()=>t.scrollIntoView({block:`start`})),c.hash=t.id)}history.replaceState(null,``,c.toString()),document.dispatchEvent(new Event(`reading-mode-change`))})})});</script><nav class="story-toc" aria-label="In this story" data-layer="fact"><details class="toc-disclosure" open><summary><span>In this story</span><span class="toc-current" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><ol><li><a href="#what-happened">What happened</a></li><li><a href="#the-catch">The catch</a></li><li><a href="#where-this-sits">Where this sits</a></li><li><a href="#who-feels-it">Who feels it</a></li><li><a href="#outlets">What the coverage got right, and what it got wrong</a></li><li><a href="#claim-check">Claim checked against the record</a></li><li><a href="#what-happened-next">What happened next</a></li><li><a href="#unknowns">What we do not know yet</a></li><li><a href="#records">The records</a></li></ol></details></nav><div class="kpi-strip" data-layer="fact"><div class="kpi"><span class="kpi-value">&gt;30<small> days</small></span><span class="kpi-label">Notice before a covered change</span></div><div class="kpi"><span class="kpi-value">Sept. 23<small></small></span><span class="kpi-label">Court-ordered status report</span></div><div class="kpi"><span class="kpi-value">seven days<small></small></span><span class="kpi-label">Initial temporary closure</span></div></div><aside class="three-things" data-layer="fact"><p class="tt-label">Three things to know</p><ol><li>Judge Christopher Cooper denied Representative Joyce Beatty's request for an emergency hearing on September 17. In the same minute order, he required written notice more than 30 days before the defendants implement a change to the project plans previously presented to the court, including demolition of the main building.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="more than 30 days before the implementation of any changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a></sup></li><li>The reproduced sentence does not say that every physical change is covered or state whether demolition would be lawful. It makes notice turn on changes to the scope of the project plans previously presented to the court.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a></sup></li><li>The executive director said the immediate closure was a seven-day safety measure unless extended. The defendants characterized it as separate from the board's renovation decision.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-5" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17/" data-passage="which will last for seven days, unless extended" aria-label="Source 5: read the evidence">5</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-4" data-record-href="/records/defendants-response-86-2026-09-17/" data-passage="separate from any Board decision related to closure for ongoing renovations" aria-label="Source 4: read the evidence">4</a></sup></li></ol></aside><p class="railed rail-note" data-layer="fact">The federal docket's September 17 minute order was not available as a court-hosted document in the public sources we could preserve. UPI reproduces the operative sentence below in full. Beatty's counsel quotes part of it and describes the requirement as 30 days' advance warning; the surrounding motions, declarations, earlier opinions and board records are preserved separately.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-18" data-record-href="/records/beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17/" data-passage="any changes to the scope of the project plans" aria-label="Source 18: read the evidence" data-passages="30 days’ advance warning">18</a></sup></p><div data-layer="proof" class="event-record-context"><p class="sources-line">This story rests on filings in Beatty v. Trump and D.C. Preservation League v. Trump; the court's May 29 opinions; the board's August meeting record; the August 28 joint report; the September 16 scheduling order; federal statutes governing the Kennedy Center; the September 17 minute order as reproduced in full by UPI and quoted in part by Beatty's counsel; and the coverage records checked against those documents.</p></div><section id="what-happened"><p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The request and the ruling</p><h2 data-layer="fact">The judge refused the hearing and added an advance-notice rule</h2><p data-layer="narrative">Beatty asked for an emergency hearing after the main building closed and after the board voted to close it for renovation. The defendants answered that the immediate closure was separate from the renovation decision. Executive Director Matt Floca described it as a temporary safety measure and declared that structural deterioration created acute risks to public safety. He said the initial closure would last seven days unless extended.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-1" data-record-href="/records/beatty-motion-84-2026-09-16/" data-passage="MOTION FOR EMERGENCY HEARING" aria-label="Source 1: read the evidence">1</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-4" data-record-href="/records/defendants-response-86-2026-09-17/" data-passage="separate from any Board decision related to closure for ongoing renovations" aria-label="Source 4: read the evidence">4</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-5" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17/" data-passage="acute risks to public safety resulting from continued structural deterioration" aria-label="Source 5: read the evidence" data-passages="which will last for seven days, unless extended">5</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">The filing also put two public signals before Cooper. Trump had told reporters that without recognition for his administration's role in the renovation and fundraising, the building would close and end up being ripped down. The filing included a photograph of hi
