pi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="more than 30 days before the implementation of any changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a></sup></p></div></div></section><section id="what-happened-next"><p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The next dated steps</p><h2 data-layer="fact">The closure and renovation claims moved onto separate tracks</h2><p data-layer="narrative">The existing scheduling order had already opened expedited discovery on Beatty's closure claim. It set September 23 deadlines for written discovery requests and deposition notices, September 30 for written responses, October 7 for completed depositions and October 9 for the close of discovery.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-15" data-record-href="/records/scheduling-order-82-2026-09-16/" data-passage="Requests for Written and Document Discovery" aria-label="Source 15: read the evidence" data-passages="All Discovery Closed">15</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">The September 17 order added the update and advance-notice requirements. The September 16 scheduling order separately set deadlines for a motion to vacate the preliminary injunction and for discovery on the closure claim.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-18" data-record-href="/records/beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17/" data-passage="required the Board to update the Court by September 23" aria-label="Source 18: read the evidence">18</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="more than 30 days before the implementation" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-15" data-record-href="/records/scheduling-order-82-2026-09-16/" data-passage="Motion to Vacate the Preliminary" aria-label="Source 15: read the evidence">15</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">On September 18, the defendants filed a motion to dissolve the May preliminary injunction and a renewed motion for partial summary judgment on Beatty's remaining closure and construction claims. Those motions asked the court for relief; they did not themselves dissolve the injunction or decide the claims.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-24" data-record-href="/records/defendants-motion-vacate-88-2026-09-18/" data-passage="DEFENDANTS’ MOTION TO DISSOLVE PRELIMINARY INJUNCTION" aria-label="Source 24: read the evidence">24</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-25" data-record-href="/records/defendants-summary-judgment-89-2026-09-18/" data-passage="DEFENDANTS’ RENEWED MOTION FOR" aria-label="Source 25: read the evidence">25</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">Floca says management distributed a packet on September 13 for discussion at the September 15 board meeting and attached it to his declaration as Exhibit B. The declaration dates the packet to the closure deliberations but does not reproduce its contents or identify the recognition proposal.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-29" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-89-3-2026-09-18/" data-passage="On September 13, 2026, the Center distributed to trustees a packet of materials" aria-label="Source 29: read the evidence" data-passages="attached to this declaration as Exhibit B">29</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">The defense filings agree that the board voted again to close the main building, but they quote the timing differently. The statement of facts says it would close to patrons immediately; the supporting memorandum says closure would follow dissolution of the preliminary injunction.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-28" data-record-href="/records/defendants-statement-facts-89-2-2026-09-18/" data-passage="shall be closed to patrons forthwith" aria-label="Source 28: read the evidence">28</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-27" data-record-href="/records/defendants-consolidated-memorandum-88-1-2026-09-18/" data-passage="forthwith upon the dissolution of the preliminary injunction" aria-label="Source 27: read the evidence">27</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">The defendants argued that phased closure would create a $300 million funding shortfall, compared with less than $30 million for full closure. These were the defendants' assertions. Floca's declaration identifies an earlier JLL plan and Delta presentation as filed under seal. It says the finalized Delta report and certain appendices were attached as Exhibit A, while appendices with sensitive architectural drawings were excluded.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-27" data-record-href="/records/defendants-consolidated-memorandum-88-1-2026-09-18/" data-passage="a $300 million funding shortfall" aria-label="Source 27: read the evidence">27</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-29" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-89-3-2026-09-18/" data-passage="appears under seal on the docket" aria-label="Source 29: read the evidence" data-passages="correct copy of that report and certain of its appendices is attached to this declaration as&#10;appendices that contain sensitive architectural drawings">29</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">Later on September 18, thousands joined the Hands Around the Kennedy Center protest, and some formed a human chain around the building. The organizer invited artists, patrons, staff members, union members and volunteers.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-33" data-record-href="/records/ap-kennedy-center-protest-2026-09-18/" data-passage="Thousands of people joined outside" aria-label="Source 33: read the evidence" data-passages="formed a human chain around the center">33</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-34" data-record-href="/records/action-network-hands-around-kennedy-center-2026-09-18/" data-passage="Worked at the Center as a staff member, union member, or volunteer" aria-label="Source 34: read the evidence">34</a></sup></p></section><section id="unknowns"><p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">Open questions</p><h2 data-layer="fact">What we do not know yet</h2><ul data-layer="fact"><li data-absence>Whether the September 23 status report was filed, and whether the initial safety closure was extended. Searched: the admitted docket material and coverage through September 19; the report was not yet due.</li><li data-absence>Whether the defendants have developed a project-scope change that would trigger the notice order. The accessible public filings through September 19 do not identify an approved demolition plan. Floca's declaration identifies an earlier JLL report and Delta presentation filed under seal. It says the finalized Delta report and certain appendices were filed as Exhibit A, but that exhibit did not answer through the public docket route.</li><li data-absence>Which closure condition appears in the September 15 preliminary minutes. The two defense filings quote the resolution differently, and the preliminary minutes were not available through the public docket route.</li><li>Trump's intent remained unresolved on September 18. The Associated Press reported that he did not directly respond when asked whether he planned to demolish the theater.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-35" data-record-href="/records/ap-trump-kennedy-center-2026-09-18/" data-passage="did not directly respond when a reporter asked whether he planned to demolish the theater" aria-label="Source 35: read the evidence">35</a></sup></li><li data-absence>The court's minute order as a standalone, court-hosted document. Searched: the District Court docket, CourtListener and Justia; the docket routes were unavailable to the capture registry and the Justia mirror stopped before September 17. The page therefore labels the carriers of the quoted sentence.</li></ul></section><section id="records" data-layer="fact"><p class="sec-kicker">Sources</p><h2>The records</h2><p class="section-lede">Everything this page rests on, numbered where the story cites it. We keep a dated copy of each one.</p><h3 class="src-group">Primary documents</h3><ol class="src-list" start="1"><li id="src-1" value="1"><a href="/records/beatty-motion-84-2026-09-16/">Plaintiff motion for an emergency hearing</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-16 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; Beatty’s request for an emergency hearing over the closure</span></li><li id="src-2" value="2"><a href="/records/kennedy-bailey-declaration-84-1-2026-09-16/">Declaration of Bridget Kennedy-Bailey</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-16 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; firsthand observations submitted with the emergency motion</span></li><li id="src-3" value="3"><a href="/records/beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17/">Notice of supplemental authority</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the demolition placard and statements put before the court</span></li><li id="src-4" value="4"><a href="/records/defendants-response-86-2026-09-17/">Defendants’ response to the emergency-hearing motion</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the defendants’ account of the temporary closure</span></li><li id="src-5" value="5"><a href="/records/floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17/">Declaration of Charles Matthew Floca</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the sworn safety basis and initial duration of the closure</span></li><li id="src-6" value="6"><a href="/records/beatty-reply-87-2026-09-17/">Plaintiff’s reply in support of an emergency hearing</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; Beatty’s chronology supporting her pretext argument about the temporary closure</span></li><li id="src-7" value="7"><a href="/records/preservation-joint-report-62-2026-08-28/">Joint meet-and-confer report</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-08-28 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the defendants’ no-demolition and no-new-structure position</span></li><li id="src-8" value="8"><a href="/records/preservation-addendum-62-1-2026-08-28/">Preservation plaintiffs’ addendum</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-08-28 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the preservation plaintiffs’ contemporaneous response</span></li><li id="src-9" value="9"><a href="/records/preservation-opinion-45-2026-05-29/">Memorandum opinion in D.C. Preservation League v. Trump</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-05-29 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the September 2025 renovation announcement and the represented project scope</span></li><li id="src-10" value="10"><a href="/records/beatty-opinion-50-2026-05-29/">Memorandum opinion in Beatty v. Trump</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-05-29 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the closure baseline, employee estimate and practical effects identified in the record</span></li><li id="src-11" value="11"><a href="/records/beatty-opinion-77-2026-09-15/">Memorandum opinion on the proposed recognition additions</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-15 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the September 15 ruling preceding the closure dispute</span></li><li id="src-12" value="12"><a href="/records/board-resolution-66-2-2026-08-13/">Kennedy Center board resolution on recognition additions</a> · Kennedy Center Board of Trustees, 2026-08-13 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the board’s separate recognition proposal</span></li><li id="src-13" value="13"><a href="/records/board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13/">Kennedy Center board meeting minutes</a> · Kennedy Center Board of Trustees, 2026-08-13 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the closure resolution, vote and acknowledged gaps in the decision materials</span></li><li id="src-14" value="14"><a href="/records/board-vote-notice-78-2026-09-15/">Notice of the September 15 board vote</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-15 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the second board action before the emergency motion</span></li><li id="src-15" value="15"><a href="/records/scheduling-order-82-2026-09-16/">Scheduling order for expedited closure discovery</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-16 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the deadlines for the closure claim</span></li><li id="src-18" value="18"><a href="/records/beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17/">Beatty counsel reaction to the notice order</a> · Washington Litigation Group, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; a party c
