all rights in the event that Defendants’ plans change or work commences at the Center without the

Beatty injunction having been dissolved.

       The parties therefore request that the Court stay discovery and the parties’ Rule 26 and

Local Rule 16.3 submissions until the Court rules on Defendants’ forthcoming motion to dissolve

the injunction entered in the Beatty matter, or until further order of the Court. The parties propose

to submit a meet-and-confer report addressing the topics set forth in the Court’s August 7, 2026

Order within fourteen days of the Court’s ruling on Defendants’ forthcoming motion to dissolve

the preliminary injunction in the Beatty matter, with a scheduling conference to be held thereafter

at the Court’s convenience.




