55:      <p class="railed rail-note" data-layer="fact">The federal docket's September 17 minute order was not available as a court-hosted document in the public sources we could preserve. UPI reproduces the operative sentence below in full. Beatty's counsel quotes part of it and describes the requirement as 30 days' advance warning; the surrounding motions, declarations, earlier opinions and board records are preserved separately.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events" /><Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="any changes to the scope of the project plans" /><Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="30 days’ advance warning" /></p>
