89-        <p data-layer="narrative">The parties' August 28 joint report made the relevant promise explicit: the defendants would inform the plaintiffs and the court if the board's plans reversed the position that the building would not be demolished and no new structure would be built.<Cite s="preservation-joint-report-62-2026-08-28" passage="Defendants have pledged to inform Plaintiffs and the Court" /><Cite s="preservation-joint-report-62-2026-08-28" passage="building will not be demolished and that no new structure will be constructed" /></p>
90-        <p data-layer="narrative">Congress appropriated about {funding.appropriationLabel} for capital repair, restoration, the maintenance backlog and security structures, with the money available through {funding.availabilityDeadline}.<Cite s="public-law-119-21-kennedy-center" passage="$256,657,000, to remain" /><Cite s="public-law-119-21-kennedy-center" passage="available until September 30, 2029" /></p>
91:        <p data-layer="narrative">The August minutes say that keeping the main building partly open would leave the appropriation covering only about half of the work, with a {funding.partialOperationShortfallLabel} shortfall after utilities. The minutes put the closure estimate at about {funding.closureEstimateLabel}.<Cite s="board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13" passage="would cover only approximately half of the work" /><Cite s="board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13" passage="shortfall of $124M" /><Cite s="board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13" passage="approximately $285 million" /></p>
92-        <figure class="story-figure" data-layer="fact"><figcaption><strong>How the notice order arose</strong><span>The dated sequence in the court and board records.</span></figcaption><DecisionTimeline entries={timeline} /><p class="chart-source">The first entry comes from the court's account of the Center announcing that renovation work had begun. The same record defines the REACH as the Center's expansion campus.<Cite s="preservation-opinion-45-2026-05-29" passage="work has begun!" /><Cite s="beatty-opinion-50-2026-05-29" passage="expansion campus, known as the REACH" /></p></figure>
93-      </section>
