NO-SHIP. Ranked findings:

1. **Major: The page implies the order contains no discovery provision, but the full order expressly permits discovery.**

   - Page bytes at offsets 15,866, 16,232, and 40,030: “Beatty's counsel said Cooper ‘ordered discovery into the Board’s actions related to a potential demolition.’” “UPI's reproduced order text contains the notice command but no discovery provision.” “The September 17 order added the update and advance-notice requirements.” [Built HTML](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/dist/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition/index.html:2>)
   - Record bytes: “Finally, Plaintiff may seek discovery regarding the subject of their 85 Notice of Supplemental Authority to the extent permitted by the Federal Rules and the Court's scheduling order.” [September 17 minute order](https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/72069932/beatty-v-trump/?order_by=desc#minute-entry-478383984)
   - Correct account: Cooper permitted Beatty to seek discovery concerning the supplemental notice, bounded by the Federal Rules and the existing scheduling order. Counsel's “ordered discovery” wording is broader than the order, but the page uses an incomplete UPI excerpt to suggest the provision is absent when the primary record confirms it.

2. **Minor: The quotation attributed to Cooper contains UPI's editorial insertions.**

   - Page bytes at offset 14,788: “The Court hereby ORDERS Defendants [the Kennedy Center board] ... D.C. Preservation League [a separate case] ...” [Built HTML](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/dist/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition/index.html:2>)
   - Record bytes: “The Court hereby ORDERS Defendants to provide such notice ... presented to the Court in D.C. Preservation League, including but not limited to any ‘demolition’ of the Center's main building.” The two bracketed explanations do not appear in the order. [September 17 minute order](https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/72069932/beatty-v-trump/?order_by=desc#minute-entry-478383984)
   - Correct account: The bracketed phrases are UPI's glosses, not Cooper's words. They may be retained as explicitly identified editorial annotations, but they should not appear as an unqualified judicial quotation when the primary text is available.

3. **Minor: “No-demolition position” is wider than the position on which the court relied.**

   - Page bytes at offsets 18,358 and 25,614: “The court had relied on a no-demolition position” and “reversal of the no-demolition position.” [Built HTML](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/dist/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition/index.html:2>)
   - Record bytes: “full demolition and a ‘Complete Rebuilding’ are not in the cards.” [Preservation opinion](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/data/sources/kennedy-center/preservation-opinion-45-2026-05-29.txt:960>) The companion opinion says “demolition and structural steel reconfiguration” would occur elsewhere and anticipates “demolition and reconfiguration of component parts.” [Beatty opinion](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/data/sources/kennedy-center/beatty-opinion-50-2026-05-29.txt:4011>)
   - Correct account: The representation excluded razing or fully rebuilding the main building. It did not exclude demolition of stage floors or other component parts during renovation.

4. **Minor: The account of the August operating plan omits continued public access to the Kennedy memorial.**

   - Page bytes at offset 27,517 list REACH programming, off-site National Symphony performances, the Honors, and the Mark Twain Prize, but not the memorial. [Built HTML](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/dist/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition/index.html:2>)
   - Record bytes: “the Memorial to President John F. Kennedy be temporarily relocated to the REACH where it will remain open to the public.” [Board minutes](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/data/sources/kennedy-center/board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13.txt:632>)
   - Correct account: The plan also moved the presidential memorial to the REACH and promised that it would remain publicly accessible during the main-building closure.

5. **Minor: The page uses the protest record for attendance but omits its concrete account of consequences for local arts students.**

   - Page bytes at offset 44,165: “thousands joined ... some formed a human chain ... The organizer invited artists, patrons, staff members, union members and volunteers.” [Built HTML](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/dist/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition/index.html:2>)
   - Record bytes: Alina Baciu described Duke Ellington students borrowing Washington National Opera costumes and performing on the Millennium Stage, then said, “All of those things have gone away.” [AP protest record](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/data/sources/coverage/kennedy-center/ap-kennedy-center-protest-2026-09-18.txt:16>)
   - Correct account: The record identifies students as an affected constituency and describes lost costume access and performance opportunities, not merely generalized concern among protesters.

6. **Minor: A stranger cannot tell what the “three recognition proposals” were.**

   - Page bytes at offsets 35,679 and 36,046 say “all three recognition proposals were shot down,” then correct the disposition without defining the proposals. [Built HTML](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/dist/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition/index.html:2>)
   - Record bytes: The proposals were a “renovated and restored by President Donald J. Trump” inscription, a second inscription conditional on the Trump Kennedy Center Fund reaching $100 million, and renaming the grounds “President Donald J. Trump Plaza.” [Board resolution](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/data/sources/kennedy-center/board-resolution-66-2-2026-08-13.txt:32>) The court enjoined the first and third and denied the conditional endowment-inscription request as unripe. [September 15 opinion](</Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-sol/data/sources/kennedy-center/beatty-opinion-77-2026-09-15.txt:426>)
   - Correct account: Name the three proposals before explaining their different dispositions. Otherwise the correction is accurate but not independently understandable.

VERDICT: NO-SHIP


